Article 26

1. The Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women and children.
2. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and e. evaluation.
3. Supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), is conducted with the principles of: a. professional;

b. transparent; and
c. accountable.

