h. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; andi. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 5

Children, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, also receive special rights, as follows:
a. right to respect and full use for survival, growth, development and participation;
b. right to basic services;
c. right to equal protection;
d. right to be free from various stigma; ande. right to obtain freedom.

