CHAPTER XII

INVESTIGATION

Article 33

1. In addition to general investigation officers, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation, Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children may also be carried out by Civil Servant Investigators (PPNS) as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Law.
2. PPNS as referred to in paragraph (1), are certain civil servant officials within the Regional Government who are appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
3. In carrying out investigation duties, PPNS as referred to in paragraph (2), are authorized to: a. receive reports or complaints from someone about the existence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;
c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identification;
d. seize objects and/or documents;
e. take fingerprints and photograph a person;
f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in experts needed in connection with case examination;
h. stop the investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident is not a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the Public Prosecutor, the suspect or their family; and/or i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
4. PPNS as referred to in paragraph (2), notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Police Investigator Officer of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law.

